  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 311 AM CDT Wed Sep 23 2026\n\nNo significant changes to the extended forecast with this package.\nA moist southwesterly flow pattern aloft will continue into\nfriday, with a continued chance of showers and thunderstorms\npersisting over much of our region, with the highest chances\nremaining focused over our western and northwestern CWA. We will\nneed to continue monitoring for additional heavy rainfall and\nflooding concerns Friday into Friday night. The mid-level flow\npattern transitions more zonal on Saturday with the axis of\nmoisture and associated rain/storm chances becoming more focused\nover southern portions of our forecast area Saturday afternoon and\nevening. Upper ridging briefly builds back over west Texas and\nsoutheast New Mexico Sunday into Monday, so storm chances will\ntrend lower both of these days (best chance focused over the\nsouthwest mountains). The next shortwave trough brings an\nincreasing chance of showers and thunderstorms and perhaps some\npotential for locally heavy rainfall over the area again late\nMonday into Tuesday. A warming trend otherwise occurs late this\nweekend into early next week with highs reaching back into the\nupper 80s to mid 90s over much of our area.",
